        "--help"
      ],
      "exit": 0,
      "stdout": "Compile graphs and stage or apply native publication plans\n\nUsage: rulette transform [OPTIONS] [INPUT]...\n\nArguments:\n  [INPUT]...\n          Explicit snapshot files, directories, tar archives, or gzip-compressed tar archives.\n          \n          Use `-` for one explicitly selected tar, gzip-compressed tar, graph JSON, or graph TOML stream. Plain native stdin is rejected because it has no naming and layout contract.\n\nOptions:\n      --from <FROM>\n          Select one homogeneous source decoder; `auto` accepts only one unambiguous native frontend. Graph JSON and TOML require explicit selection\n          \n          [default: auto]\n          [possible values: auto, claude, cursor-mdc, codex, antigravity, opencode, agent-plugin, graph-json, graph-toml]\n\n  -q, --quiet\n          Suppress non-error output\n\n      --no-color\n          Disable colored output\n\n      --select <SELECT>\n          Select one package by its exact graph package ID\n\n      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>\n          Log verbosity (error, warn, info, debug, trace)\n\n      --target <TARGET>\n          Stage one or more unique native targets as `format@scope`; repeated spellings are deduplicated\n\n      --allow-lossy\n          Accept reported representational loss for requested native targets\n\n      --stage <STAGE>\n          Write a self-contained publication plan to this new directory\n\n      --project-root <PROJECT_ROOT>\n          Explicitly authorize the live project root for all project targets\n\n      --user-root <USER_ROOT>\n          Explicitly authorize one user target root as `target=path`\n\n      --check\n          Check destinations without creating a stage or applying a plan\n\n      --apply <STAGE_DIR/rulette.plan.json>\n          Apply the plan at `stage-dir/rulette.plan.json`\n\n      --expect-plan-sha256 <EXPECT_PLAN_SHA256>\n          Require this SHA-256 digest before checking or applying a staged plan\n\n      --allow-project-root <ALLOW_PROJECT_ROOT>\n          Explicitly authorize the live project root for plan operations\n\n      --allow-user-root <ALLOW_USER_ROOT>\n          Explicitly authorize one plan user target root as `target=path`\n\n      --replace\n          Allow an apply operation to replace conflicting destinations\n\n      --config <CONFIG>\n          Load one explicit selection-and-target-only transform configuration file\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\n",
